{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"8705 baseline: full suite (pytest -m 'not integration and not external' -q) running on the pre-split worktree at origin/main 3834269c53 to capture the test-count parity baseline before any edit. Reference set for the moved cluster confirmed with BOTH Serena find_referencing_symbols AND repo-wide string grep; they agree. Live consumers: src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py (passes.pass2_completion, passes.completion_floor_drop), scripts/calibrate_completion_floor.py (both, via passes.*), tests/unit/test_completion_floor.py (from ...passes import completion_floor_drop + 3 constants), tests/unit/test_plan_review_completion.py (passes.pass2_completion, passes._completion_finding_listing, passes.COMPLETION_*), tests/unit/workflow/test_review_output_budget.py (passes.pass2_completion). MONKEYPATCH FINDING: a repo-wide grep for setattr targets on the passes module object returns ONLY 'load_move_registry' and 'applicable_moves' (tests/interfaces/contracts/test_plan_review_prerequisite_isolation.py) — neither is in the moved cluster, so no existing patch seam is crossed. The function-local import is still MANDATORY here for a stronger reason than c6c9's: passes imports the new module at module level (register_contracts() runs at import time and needs _pass2_completion_model), so a module-level 'from .passes import ...' in the new module is a hard import cycle."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785912153262862001,"uuid":"f066a079-9b72-4615-91eb-d5e26473e33a"}